{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>He sent</b> — these were the ones that came before the plague of the firstborn. The yod in <b>בתוככי</b> ['in the midst of you'] faces Egypt [i.e., with final yod indicating direction]. Likewise <b>and I will rouse your sons, O Zion, against your sons, O Greece</b>." "<b>And He mentioned Pharaoh and all his servants</b> — and all the more so His people."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 135, :notes {0 "The comment begins with a gloss on שלח but the argument about the yod in בתוככי is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:45.687137969Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}